Peter durante Tommen is best known for  overhauling the PC port of Dark Souls  with dsfix a texture mod that made  significant visual improvements over the  vanilla version of the game though there  is as of yet no dsfix to Durante has  been hard at work on his latest mod the  ambitious G dosa tube or general down  sampling tool the tool enables games to  run at ridiculously high resolutions and  then down samples them to a super crisp  1080p this is only the beginning however  as the mod also adds a handful of  options for improving Dark Souls 2 s  overall appearance the most noticeable  change comes from the post-processing  option this is the equivalent of color  correcting the entirety of your Dark  Souls 2 experience colors become deeper  and more vibrant and contrast is  markedly improved with post-processing  enabled medulla feels like a sunset  drenched abandoned village instead of a  drab grey clearing with a few buildings  this effect alone is worth grabbing G  dosa to the mods anti-aliasing toggle  makes little difference when down  sampling no matter how hard you push it  but it's useful for running the game at  lower resolutions that create jaggies  and other visual aberrations otherwise  it's probably just sucking up some of  your resources and should be disabled  the depth of field option adds blur to  objects proportional to their distance  from your point of view this is  comparable to the effect of a camera  lens set to a wide aperture though some  may find it odd to consider the blurring  of objects of visual improvement shallow  depth of field lens dark souls2 a  cinematic feel and renders backdrop  elements in a dreamy haze that adds to  the mystique of drangleic the ambient  occlusion option defines how exposed  certain elements are to the ambient  lighting in an area enabling ambient  occlusion adds a touch of shadow to the  edges of objects and give us a lifelike  appearance to the finer details of the  world such as stonework statues flora  characters clothing and armor etc this  effect is resource intensive so if  you're just barely pumping out a stable  framerate this may be the option to  disable first but it is a nice touch if  you've got power to spare Dorantes G  dosa 2 is an impressive mod that renders  the PC port of Dark Souls 2 its  definitive version until dsfix 2 comes  out and for the love of God well  somebody please give Durante a job on  the next Souls game  [Music]
 

